{
  "id": "color-adaptation",
  "term": "color adaptation",
  "definition": "Color adaptation is a change in visual color perception after prolonged exposure to color-related input, so that later color judgments are biased in the opposite direction. In this source, the effect is shown not only after color experience itself but also after understanding language that strongly implies a particular color.",
